$DEF,-,<$DEC,$BAR,-,$BIN,~1;,$BIN,~2;;;>;
Long long ago in ancient Hanoi, priests were asked to move 64 jade
disks from one peg to another. The disks were so precious and fragile,
that it was unthinkable to place a larger disk on top of a smaller 
one. Fortunately, they had a 3rd peg.
$REM,<
# Python solution
def move(v, fro, to, mid):
    if v:
        move(v-1, fro, mid, to)
        print(v, fro, to)
        move(v-1, mid, to, fro)
move(int(input()), 1, 3, 2)
>;
$DEF,H,<$~1,~2,~3,~4,$DEF,~1,<$H,$-,~0,1;,~1,~3,~2;Move disk ~0 from tower ~1 to tower ~2
$H,$-,~0,1;,~3,~2,~1;>;$DEF,0,;;>;

$H,3,1,2,3;

As a world heritage site, the original towers of Hanoi underwent
restoration. During this difficult time the direct movement of disks between
peg 1 and peg 3 was not allowed.

$REM,<
# Python solution
def move(v, fro, to, mid):
    if v:
         if mid == 2:
            move(v-1, fro, to, mid)
            print(v, fro, mid)
            move(v-1, to, fro, mid)
            print(v, mid, to)
            move(v-1, fro, to, mid)
         else:
            move(v-1, fro, mid, to)
            print(v, fro, to)
            move(v-1, mid, to, fro) 
move(int(input()), 1, 3, 2)
>;

$DEF,H,<$~1x~3,~1,~2,~3,~4,$DEF,~1x~3,<$H,$-,~1,1;,~2,~4,~3;Move disk ~1 from tower ~2 to tower ~4
$H,$-,~1,1;,~3,~2,~4;>;$DEF,~1x2,<$H,$-,~1,1;,~2,~3,~4;Move disk ~1 from tower ~2 to tower ~3
$H,$-,~1,1;,~4,~3,~2;Move disk ~1 from tower ~3 to tower ~4
$H,$-,~1,1;,~2,~3,~4;>;$DEF,0x~3,;;>;
$H,3,1,2,3;

$REM,<
The popularity of the tower of Hanoi had grown so much that the priest
had established one-way traffic around the tower. Now, the disks from
peg 1 can be moved only to peg 2; the disks from peg 2 -- to peg 3;
and the disks from peg 3 -- to peg 1.

$REM,<
# Python solution
n=int(input())
def foo(v,fro,to,mid):
    if v:
        next=fro%3+1
        if next==to:
            foo(v-1,fro,mid,to)
            print(v,fro,to)
            foo(v-1,mid,to,fro)
        else:
            foo(v-1,fro,to,mid)
            print(v,fro,mid)
            foo(v-1,to,fro,mid)
            print(v,mid,to)
            foo(v-1,fro,to,mid)
foo(n,1,3,2)
>;

$DEF,N,<$+$%~1,3;,1;>
$DEF,H,<$~1x~3,~1,~2,~3,~4,$DEF,~1x~3,<$H,$-,~1,1;,~2,~4,~3;Move disk ~1 from tower ~2 to tower ~4
$H,$-,~1,1;,~3,~2,~4;>;$DEF,0x~3,;;>;
>;

The new chief prist, on his whim, has prohibited to place the smallest
disk on the middle peg.
$REM,<
# Python solution
def move(v, fro, to, mid):
    if v == 1:
        print(v, fro, to)
    else:
        move(v-1, fro, to, mid)
        print(v, fro, mid)
        move(v-1, to, fro, mid)
        print(v, mid, to)
        move(v-1, fro, to, mid)
move(int(input()), 1, 3, 2)
>;
$DEF,H,<$~1,~2,~3,~4,$DEF,~1,<$H,$-,~0,1;,~1,~2,~3;Move disk ~0 from tower ~1 to tower ~2
$H,$-,~0,1;,~3,~2,~1;Move disk ~0 from tower ~2 to tower ~3
